* ''One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"it's the only way to retain control over faces that don't know about each other"//). Each face's PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, its event store, its registry, its archive and its content-key seat; no vessel-wide identity registers a face's bags, delegates them, or holds a face's group. Two faces of one vessel then never link on the wire, a removal from one face rolls that face's bags alone, and a bundle restores one face and nothing of another. The tree holds `K15`'s steps 0 to 3 and 6, as read in code (one hearth observation still owed): a face's hive stands on its own atom, its own event-store scope and its own face door (`makeFaceBagDoor`), and the vessel identity registers only vessel-ground bags; the research meme records the earlier measure (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/keyhive-per-persona-group-2026`>>). House readings under the operator's confidence, each naming what flips it: a herm keeps a floor-only transport key, behind a red test that it can neither author, resolve nor observe a face's capabilities, and holds no Keyhive identity if that test fails; several face hives share one process only after a substrate probe reads them isolated, and each face's hive runs in its own worker otherwise; co-mingled history migrates by fresh identities and an old mixed archive refuses by name, with no bridge; a founder that cannot leave its group leaves by a fresh PersonaGroup. Item `K15` carries the build, folding `W25` and `K12`; `W26`'s slice 3 waits on its face context.

